{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll 3 tests pass. Here's a summary of the SQLAlchemy 2.x modernization:\n\n**`app/repository.py`**\n- Replaced `session.query()` with `select()` statements\n- Removed `session.commit()` from helpers; callers now manage transactions\n\n**`app/worker.py`**\n- Uses `select()` for queries\n- Single transaction boundary: all changes commit only if no exception occurs\n- On failure, the context manager automatically rolls back (e.g., `settle_entry` leaves status as `\"pending\"` not `\"processing\"`)\n\n**`app/admin_cli.py`**\n- Uses `select()` for queries  \n- Dry-run mode restores original values and calls `session.rollback()` to ensure no persistence\n- Non-dry-run commits all changes atomically\n\n**`app/api.py`**\n- Replaced `session.query()` with `select()`\n- No longer relies on repository functions that commit; callers control transactions\n\n**`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`**\n- Updated to document the new transaction boundary semantics"}}
